WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.000
Harry Kersh: From a gravy
pizza to a pint of frosting,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.370
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.920
between seasonal fast-food menus

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.500
in the UK and the US.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.310
Let's start with McDonald's.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.310
Now, they've gone quite big

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.802
and added five seasonal
items to their menu.

00:00:20.802 --> 00:00:23.100
Joe Avella: McDonald's in the
US only has two menu items,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.310
and actually one of
them isn't very festive.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:27.060
This thing is itching me
and making a lot of noise,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.400
so I'm taking it off.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.680
Santa Claus, you got it.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.996
In the US, McDonald's has

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:33.287
the holiday pie and the McRib.

00:00:33.287 --> 00:00:34.310
Harry: Now, let's start with what, for me,

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.260
is probably the main event,

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.460
which is this: the double Big Mac.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.580
Now, I have a couple of
reservations about this burger.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.037
No. 1, I'm not sure what
makes it Christmassy,

00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:43.338
and No. 2, I'm not sure

00:00:43.338 --> 00:00:44.763
you can really call it a double Big Mac

00:00:44.763 --> 00:00:46.920
unless it is actually
double the weight and size

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.643
of a regular Big Mac.

00:00:48.643 --> 00:00:50.316
I mean, it is kinda tall.

00:00:52.672 --> 00:00:54.371
About 275.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.100
So, it's actually only a 30% increase

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.370
if you get the double Big Mac,

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.860
which, as I suspected,
is far from doubling it.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.850
Joe: Harry, I feel you
on that double Big Mac,

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.940
so I'm gonna make one of my own

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.140
and see exactly what you're
working with over there.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.280
One piece of bread in the middle.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.670
The middle piece of bread's
always really strange.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:16.627
I mean, this is looking,

00:01:16.627 --> 00:01:18.560
this is actually looking
pretty good, right?

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.963
Let's see how much it weighs!

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.070
280 grams?

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.400
Harry: McDonald's, I'm a bit disappointed,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.110
'cause you've advertised
this as a double Big Mac,

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.810
but you've only given us 30% more.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.730
So what we're going to do now

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:34.055
is make our own double
Big Mac, the official way.

00:01:36.389 --> 00:01:37.422
Ta-da.

00:01:51.864 --> 00:01:53.022
Joe: [mumbling]

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.472
That's a big mouthful.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.040
Harry: Now, the other
seasonal sandwich item

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.757
on the McDonald's menu is this,

00:01:59.757 --> 00:02:01.840
the jerk chicken sandwich.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.660
Now, in this burger, you'll
find two chicken strips,

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.340
some bacon, some cheese, some lettuce,

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.860
some onions, and a spicy jerk sauce.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.080
Next up, we have these things,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.630
which are cheese melt dippers.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.463
These come in portions of four

00:02:15.463 --> 00:02:17.420
or as a share box of 12,

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.550
and it's basically like
a breaded and fried bite

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.790
of Camembert cheese.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.890
On the dessert menu, we have
a Celebrations McFlurry,

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.570
which is a nod to Britain's obsession

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.810
with chocolate selection
boxes around Christmastime.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.120
Now, Celebrations is
Mars' addition to this,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.670
and what they have in here

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.812
is Galaxy, Twix, Mars,

00:02:34.812 --> 00:02:37.103
Snickers, and Maltesers.

00:02:37.103 --> 00:02:38.810
Joe: Uh, of those candy
bars that you mentioned,

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.370
I've heard of two of them.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.890
One of them was Twix, but besides that,

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.330
I'm not familiar with a
lot of those candy bars,

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.103
so maybe we should do a "Food
Wars" candy bars episode.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.510
Harry: Finally, McDonald's
offers a salted caramel latte.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.260
One thing to note is
that the anticaking agent

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.260
used in the caramel sugar for this latte

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.840
is calcium silicate.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.390
Now, this is fairly commonly used in food.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.250
However, it's also one of the most popular

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.710
fireproofing materials,

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.600
and it's also used to neutralize acids

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.803
that leak out of mines.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.270
Joe: The McRib. I have
no idea why the McRib

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:12.134
is during this holiday
season at McDonald's.

00:03:12.134 --> 00:03:13.720
I think what they do with the McRib

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.290
is they pretty much liquefy the meat,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.463
then pour it into a rib-shaped mold.

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:23.083
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah. Mm.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.626
Harry: KFC in the UK only has one

00:03:28.626 --> 00:03:31.201
exclusive seasonal menu
item, and it is this.

00:03:31.201 --> 00:03:33.320
This is the gravy burger box meal.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.950
This is a combo meal in which you get

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.550
a regular portion of fries,

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.140
a single chicken fillet, some gravy,

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.610
gravynaise, which is a
new addition to the menu

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.610
which is a kind of gravy
and mayo combination,

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.510
and then the main event is the burger.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.650
So what they've done here
is taken a fillet burger,

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:49.920
put some cheese on it,

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.850
and then on top of it,
it's got a hash brown.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.960
They've kind of put, like, a divot in it.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.790
And the idea is that you pour
the gravy straight on that,

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.800
and it kind of collects it in a pool.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.108
In this, there are 1,215 calories,

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.783
which is quite a lot,

00:04:03.783 --> 00:04:05.210
and I'm not sure how this is the case,

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.377
but this is actually more calories

00:04:09.617 --> 00:04:11.538
than a 14-piece bargain bucket.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.590
Joe: I love that reservoir.
That's such a good idea.

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.870
That innovation, is that only in the UK?

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.020
That's fantastic.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.310
Here in the US, our KFC
actually doesn't have

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.870
any exclusive menu items.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.120
We do, however, have this,

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.320
an exclusive KFC festive bowl.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.756
My boy Colonel's wearing
a hat similar to mine.

00:04:30.756 --> 00:04:32.599
What else is on here?

00:04:32.599 --> 00:04:34.210
Cursive fonts, that's holiday.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.893
Got the ornaments.

00:04:36.893 --> 00:04:37.943
But that's it.

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:39.738
Oh, wait, I almost forgot.

00:04:41.987 --> 00:04:43.020
Bam!

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.470
Look at this thing! You know what this is?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.561
Do you guys know what
this is? Look at this.

00:04:46.561 --> 00:04:48.747
So, this yule log smells exa--

00:04:48.747 --> 00:04:51.330
get this lame-ass bucket out of my way.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:56.330
This smells exactly
like KFC fried chicken.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.490
Do you put it in the fire with the paper?

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:58.348
How does this work?

00:04:58.348 --> 00:04:59.320
[sniffing]

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.903
No, it doesn't...

00:05:00.903 --> 00:05:02.061
I think the burning of it

00:05:02.061 --> 00:05:03.220
is crucial for it to smell.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.870
It doesn't smell like...

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.943
oh, hang on.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.262
Yeah, it doesn't...

00:05:08.262 --> 00:05:10.480
OK, so it doesn't smell
like fried chicken now,

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.390
but I'm gonna take this home,

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.330
I'm gonna throw it on my
grill, I'm gonna light it up.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.725
My whole neighborhood is gonna smell

00:05:14.725 --> 00:05:16.228
like fried chicken thanks to me.

00:05:16.228 --> 00:05:18.830
That's gonna be my holiday
gift to my neighborhood.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:22.283
The gift of things smelling like things.

00:05:28.098 --> 00:05:29.410
Harry: Now, if there's
one chain you can count on

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.760
to go all out for the
holidays, it's Starbucks.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.710
Let's take a look at some of
their exclusive menu items,

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:37.170
starting with the drinks.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.890
Now, Starbucks UK has added four drinks

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.430
to its seasonal menu, and
we'll start on this side.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:43.960
This is a truffle deluxe hot chocolate.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.410
This is a gingerbread latte,

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.810
which is festive for obvious reasons.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.020
This is an eggnog latte.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.830
Now, I've never actually tried eggnog.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.220
And then finally we
have a toffee nut latte.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.710
Again, not hugely sure
how this is festive,

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.440
but I like toffee, I like nuts,

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.803
sounds like my kind of drink.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:04.863
Ooh.

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.310
Joe: See, the thing about eggnog is

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:09.700
every year I look forward
to the holiday season

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.555
when I finally get my hands on some 'nog.

00:06:11.555 --> 00:06:13.990
And then, like clockwork, I
have, like, a couple sips,

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.820
and then I realize why
I didn't think of eggnog

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.250
for the past 11 months,

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.553
and I feel like this year
will be no different.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.273
Mm.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:25.913
I'm a 'nog head. I love eggnog.

00:06:28.369 --> 00:06:29.535
Mm.

00:06:29.535 --> 00:06:32.101
And two sips is all I can handle.

00:06:32.101 --> 00:06:33.570
Pour the rest of that in the toilet.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.580
These are the four exclusive
Starbucks holiday drinks

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.638
that we did get our hands on.

00:06:36.638 --> 00:06:37.471
They didn't label them,

00:06:37.471 --> 00:06:40.320
so I'm gonna find out in
real time what they are.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.987
It's like smelling the
cork. Just...[sniffs]

00:06:42.987 --> 00:06:45.450
I'm pretty sure this is
the toasted hot chocolate.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.210
And it's just OK.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.848
This is the -- ooh, they labeled it --

00:06:50.848 --> 00:06:53.281
the peppermint mocha Frappuccino.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:57.787
Oh, it's got bits of stuff in it.

00:06:57.787 --> 00:06:58.929
[sniffing]

00:07:01.328 --> 00:07:02.469
Ugh!

00:07:02.469 --> 00:07:04.136
Toothpastey.

00:07:04.136 --> 00:07:05.727
That's what it tastes like when,

00:07:05.727 --> 00:07:06.910
you know when you brush your teeth

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.490
and then you drink a milkshake?

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.030
That's exactly what it tastes like.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.020
[sniffing]

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:13.262
This last one, oh, God.

00:07:13.262 --> 00:07:14.686
I know which one this one is.

00:07:14.686 --> 00:07:17.740
This is a caramel brûlée latte.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.496
The caramel stuff at
Starbucks is all terrible.

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.063
Nope.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:26.640
And this is no different.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.137
Harry: Now, we love Christmas
sandwiches in the UK.

00:07:30.137 --> 00:07:31.560
A lot of the supermarket chains

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.172
will bring them out around Christmastime,

00:07:33.172 --> 00:07:34.620
and Starbucks is getting in on the act

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.270
with quite a few of its own offerings.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:37.113
Let's start with this one.

00:07:37.113 --> 00:07:39.210
This is the 'Tis the
Season turkey sandwich.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:41.480
This is the Very Merry Vegan wrap.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.480
I love the festive colors
they've got going on here.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.410
Great addition.

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:46.370
Now, this one might provoke
some philosophical questions

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.210
as to what constitutes a sandwich,

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:51.750
but this is a celebration salmon
and cream cheese croissant.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:54.310
This is the Turkey Festive Feast panini,

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:57.150
all the good stuff, no
vegetables, fantastic.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:59.430
Now, the one I'm probably most
excited to try is this one.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.920
It's The One With the
Gravy Layer sandwich.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.800
Now, if you're a fan
of the show "Friends,"

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:06.523
you might recognize this as a Moist Maker.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.770
As you can probably tell

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:14.020
by the difficulty I'm
having swallowing this,

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.320
gotta say I'm a little disappointed.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:17.650
The whole point of the "Friends" sandwich

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.500
is to add a gravy layer in the middle

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.290
that made it super moist.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.570
They've not really done
that with this one.

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:23.911
It's just three layers of bread.

00:08:23.911 --> 00:08:25.161
The ratios are all off.

00:08:25.161 --> 00:08:28.570
Joe: Over here is a cranberry bliss bar.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:32.860
You can get a whole tray
of the cranberry bliss bar.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:37.301
The toasted ham and Swiss sandwich,

00:08:37.301 --> 00:08:38.892
and of course egg.

00:08:38.892 --> 00:08:40.110
This handsome gentleman right here,

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:43.790
you got yourself a snowman-shaped cookie.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.130
It's Frosty.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.255
And if you want just the head,

00:08:48.255 --> 00:08:49.420
booyah,

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:53.910
a decapitated Frosty head on a stick.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.440
Sending a message to
the rest of the snowmen.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:59.490
Stay in line. Stay in line.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:00.863
Salted peppermint bark.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:03.744
All right?
Producer: Classic.

00:09:03.744 --> 00:09:05.752
Joe: Yeah, classic.
People seem to like these.

00:09:05.752 --> 00:09:06.973
Harry: And then, to round
out the Christmas menu

00:09:06.973 --> 00:09:09.920
from Starbucks, we have a
bunch of festive baked goods.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:10.753
We'll start on this side,

00:09:10.753 --> 00:09:13.370
with a Cranmerry cheesecake muffin.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:14.840
Bad pun. Come on, guys.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:16.570
Now, I'm not sure if
mince pies are a thing

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.530
outside of the UK,

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:21.103
or at least to the degree
they are inside the UK,

00:09:21.103 --> 00:09:23.050
but basically it's made with mincemeat,

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.760
which is not as bad as it sounds.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:28.380
It's like baked fruits that
are kind of stewed a bit.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.134
We have this adorable little guy,

00:09:31.134 --> 00:09:32.970
who's called South Pole Sam.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:34.633
I love him. He is my son.

00:09:34.633 --> 00:09:36.630
Sea-salted caramel swirl,

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.550
which, I don't know when
salted caramel became festive.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:43.010
Then we have this guy, the
Christmas tree brownie.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:44.870
And then finally we have this thing,

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:47.320
which is a raspberry and
pistachio linzer cookie.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.610
It looks like a fancy Jammie Dodger.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:50.630
Joe: I want to take this brief moment

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.510
to talk about that snowman-head cake pop

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:54.350
you saw only a moment ago.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.160
Now, I know that little guy is cute

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.040
and you wanna snack on
it this holiday season.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.450
I would be remissed if
I didn't share with you

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.910
the ingredients list.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.418
OK. Ingredients.

00:10:03.418 --> 00:10:04.551
The cake, which has sugar,

00:10:04.551 --> 00:10:06.920
enriched wheat flour,
which is wheat flour,

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.950
malted barley flour, niacin,

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:12.083
reduced iron, thiamine mononitrates,

00:10:12.083 --> 00:10:13.880
riboflavin, folic acid...

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:18.514
diglycerides, polysorbate 60, citric acid,

00:10:18.514 --> 00:10:21.550
BHT antioxidant, can we bookmark that one?

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:22.383
Thank you.

00:10:22.383 --> 00:10:24.783
Maltodextrin, annatto color extract,

00:10:24.783 --> 00:10:28.300
and potassium hydrates!

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.680
You know the one ingredient
that I bookmarked

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.540
five minutes ago, BHT?

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:35.130
That is butylated hydroxytoluene.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.250
I think that's how that's pronounced.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.520
I'm pretty sure that's
how that's pronounced.

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:38.836
If I had to say,

00:10:38.836 --> 00:10:41.511
it's buto-hauled hydro-deloc-terloserin.

00:10:41.511 --> 00:10:43.300
Studies have suggested that BHT,

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.090
along with similar chemical, BHA,

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:48.760
increase the risk of cancer in animals.

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:51.070
Woof, so even though that cake pop

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:52.820
with the little Frosty snowman hat on it

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:54.830
looks cute and fun and
your kids want to have it,

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.710
you'd be better off skipping the cake pop

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.027
and just feeding them the stick.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.103
Harry: Now let's look at
some of the best of the rest,

00:11:03.103 --> 00:11:04.710
starting with Pizza Hut.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:05.650
What Pizza Hut have done

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:08.200
is take some classic UK
Christmas dinner ingredients

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.490
and put them onto a pizza.

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.800
So, we've gone for the classic base,

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:11.633
and then on top of that,

00:11:11.633 --> 00:11:15.070
we have a red wine gravy
instead of pizza sauce.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.720
We have some cheese, some
bacon, some stuffing,

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.440
and some rotisserie chicken.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.310
The red wine base does
actually contain alcohol,

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:24.240
so there is some real red wine in there.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.408
I'm not sure how many of these

00:11:25.408 --> 00:11:27.083
you'd have to eat to get drunk.

00:11:27.083 --> 00:11:28.750
I think the grease would probably kill you

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.670
before alcohol poisoning did.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.560
Joe: I don't know what
it is about that pizza,

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:33.960
but it's incredibly depressing.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.710
Something about all the things

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:39.050
that should be at this
full family Christmas feast

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.507
all on one pizza, let's be honest,

00:11:40.507 --> 00:11:42.720
for some guy by himself, it's a bummer.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:47.050
I imagine a guy eating that
pizza alone in his apartment,

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.130
one light bulb just
swinging above his head,

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:52.010
just, like, staring out into the distance,

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.480
just no one in his life.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.307
I don't know why I'm projecting

00:11:56.307 --> 00:11:57.590
such sadness on this pizza,

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:01.390
but that is a very depressing pizza.

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:04.710
Chick-fil-A in the US has two
exclusive holiday menu items,

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:07.008
a soup, their chicken tortilla soup,

00:12:07.008 --> 00:12:10.230
and a shake, a peppermint chip shake.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:13.023
At first glance, kinda yuck.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:15.360
Smells all right,

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.426
and it comes with these

00:12:17.426 --> 00:12:20.497
crispy seasonal tortilla strips.

00:12:20.497 --> 00:12:21.970
[sighs]

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:25.400
All right, I'll try it. For you guys.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:26.323
Happy holidays.

00:12:31.293 --> 00:12:32.126
Hmm.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.742
Surprisingly not bad.

00:12:37.742 --> 00:12:39.470
That's not bad at all.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:40.450
Harry: Burger King in the UK

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:42.230
is getting involved
with their own addition,

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:44.040
which is the festive barbecue king.

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.570
However, we have a problem.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.890
Now, the one thing that was supposed

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:48.960
to make this burger festive

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.810
is the fact that it
contains five onion rings,

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:54.140
which symbolize five gold
rings from the Christmas song.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.550
However, when ours
arrived, what did we find?

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:00.790
We found one, two, three,

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.080
and maybe a half onion rings.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:04.720
That is not the song, Burger King.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.620
This is no longer a festive burger.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:07.730
You failed.

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:09.757
Joe: Dunkin' Donuts in the US does have

00:13:09.757 --> 00:13:11.532
quite a few promotional products.

00:13:11.532 --> 00:13:12.700
Four seasonal drinks,

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:13.950
seasonal sandwich,

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:17.591
and these very fun and seasonal doughnuts.

00:13:17.591 --> 00:13:19.920
Check those out. Look how fun those are.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.020
For breakfast sandwiches,

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.378
Dunkin' Donuts has this,

00:13:22.378 --> 00:13:25.050
their sourdough breakfast sandwich.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.008
And, just as advertised,

00:13:27.008 --> 00:13:29.720
two big pieces of sourdough bread,

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:33.020
eggs, bacon, cheese.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.513
Look at the size of this thing.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:39.390
Yeah, dude.

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:43.960
So, we have the signature
peppermint mocha latte.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:48.960
This is the sugarplum, I think, macchiato?

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.980
The chai latte with oat milk.

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:53.010
Don't know why that's so seasonal.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:56.403
And the gingerbread latte.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:03.215
Woof! Oh, my God!

00:14:03.215 --> 00:14:05.073
That tastes like cough syrup.

00:14:05.073 --> 00:14:07.340
No, Dunkin' Donuts. No to this.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:09.317
Get that off of your menu immediately.

00:14:09.317 --> 00:14:10.802
Bleh.

00:14:10.802 --> 00:14:12.351
[coughs]

00:14:12.351 --> 00:14:13.953
Like I said, there's three drinks.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.261
Now I know why I've never seen or heard

00:14:17.261 --> 00:14:20.340
of the sugarplum IRL till today.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.843
'Cause if that's what they taste like,

00:14:22.843 --> 00:14:24.673
they can stay in a Dickens carol.

